{"kind":"assert","text":"Reconciling the outcome of this request, with hugh's decision on 2026-10-17 (\"Delivered\").\n\nThis request's outcome reads: \"make one signing command cost much less than a cold fold of the log at this depth\". It is delivered, measured against the baseline this request recorded: a refused ratify at 54-55 s with no checkpoint, and the per-command figures in the design note (14-103 s per signing command at binary 3455950f).\n\nAfter step 2 (request d1b3d1b1, main 68fa76b3) and step 1 (request 555f239c, main 0e3b02a1), every signing command measured takes 7-10 s and makes no cold scan when a checkpoint exists. This was measured on both a frozen copy and a clone of the real artroom checkout. For example, on the real clone review-request went from 103.4 s to 9.8 s and artifact from 57.9 s to 9.8 s. At equal machine load the gain for artifact and review-request is about 5.5 times.\n\nThe remaining cost is one complete verified load of the log, which condition 2's clarification (637f7ac6) permits. Going lower would mean trusting the checkpoint in place of actor signatures, and this request keeps actor-signature verification.\n\nThe design note on request/signing-fold-once records the after-measurements and the two remaining limits: a second read for multi-act chains, and a periodic full read when a seeded submitter rebuilds checkpoint material. Landing that note closes this request."}